@host = http://localhost:8080

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 0) Health: server key (ensures Ktor is running and keys are generated)
GET {{host}}/server-key

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 1) Cast three sample votes (server encrypts one-hot u16 under election key)

### Vote A (u100 → candidate 2)
POST {{host}}/vote
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "u100",
  "name": "Alice Example",
  "address": "123 Main St",
  "age": 34,
  "candidate": 2
}

### Vote B (u101 → candidate 0)
POST {{host}}/vote
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "u101",
  "name": "Bob Example",
  "address": "45 Side St",
  "age": 41,
  "candidate": 0
}

### Vote C (u102 → candidate 3)
POST {{host}}/vote
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "u102",
  "name": "Carol Example",
  "address": "9 Elm Rd",
  "age": 29,
  "candidate": 3
}

### Inspect blocks (commitment + membership proof material)
GET {{host}}/blocks

### Raw encrypted ballots feed for the verifier (list of one-hot ciphertext lists)
GET {{host}}/user-votes

### Optional: fetch a stored per-voter receipt ciphertext (dev)
GET {{host}}/receipt/u100

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 2) MPC session — start from an uploaded per‑candidate ciphertext totals vector
### IMPORTANT: Paste the Base64 **per-candidate** tally ciphertexts you created with the CLI fold
### (the file is u16_tally_ciphertexts.json). The server will snapshot these and open a session.
POST {{host}}/mpc/sessions/start
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "source": "upload",
  "candidates": 4,
  "ctsB64": [
    /* PASTE CONTENTS OF u16_tally_ciphertexts.json HERE, e.g.
       "AAABBB...", "CCCDDD...", "EEEFFF...", "GGGHHH..."  */
  ]
}

### Capture the session id for subsequent calls
@sid = {{last_response.body.$.session.id}}

### Inspect session transcript immediately after start
GET {{host}}/mpc/sessions/{{sid}}

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 3) DEV-ONLY maskers: let the server generate/apply masks (insecure IRL, great for smoke tests)

### Participant A masks (writes verifier/sessions/<sid>/masks_A.json on disk)
POST {{host}}/mpc/sessions/{{sid}}/mask:server
Content-Type: application/json

{ "who": "A", "seed": 1234 }

### Participant B masks (writes verifier/sessions/<sid>/masks_B.json on disk)
POST {{host}}/mpc/sessions/{{sid}}/mask:server
Content-Type: application/json

{ "who": "B", "seed": 5678 }

### Check the chained masked ciphertext vector
GET {{host}}/mpc/sessions/{{sid}}

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 4) DEV-ONLY decrypt of masked totals (requires Base64 of public/u16_client_key.bin)
### ACTION: Base64-encode the file public/u16_client_key.bin and paste into clientKeyB64

POST {{host}}/mpc/sessions/{{sid}}/decrypt
Content-Type: application/json

{ "clientKeyB64": "PASTE_BASE64_OF_public/u16_client_key.bin_HERE" }

### Inspect masked plaintext totals produced by the decrypt step
GET {{host}}/mpc/sessions/{{sid}}

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 5) Reveal masks and compute final totals
### ACTION: Open verifier/sessions/<sid>/masks_A.json and masks_B.json written earlier,
###         and paste their integer arrays below in the exact order (length = candidates).

### Reveal A
POST {{host}}/mpc/sessions/{{sid}}/reveal
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "who": "A",
  "masks": [ /* paste array from masks_A.json, e.g. 123,456,789,42 */ ]
}

### Reveal B
POST {{host}}/mpc/sessions/{{sid}}/reveal
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "who": "B",
  "masks": [ /* paste array from masks_B.json */ ]
}

### Final check — totals appear once all reveals are in; finalized=true when done
GET {{host}}/mpc/sessions/{{sid}}